#!/bin/sh
# THE PUSH HOOK RUNS NOTHING, SINCE 2026-10-02 (Rob, "Option 1": the lanes are
# the gate). The door asks a pushed branch's lanes on the cluster — metered by
# daedalus, in the CI record, reused by the pull that opens on the head — so
# grading the push here too would be the second run of the same checks, and
# the unmetered one (six at once OOMKilled an engine on 2026-09-19; a
# push-stage mutation run killed node dev01 twice on 2026-10-02). main is
# still guarded: nothing lands without the pull's lanes going green.
#
# IT SAYS WHERE THE ANSWER IS, so a push that returns at once is not read as a
# push that was checked and passed. It never fails: a push is refused by the
# door or not at all.
#
# THE FILE STAYS. The spec-kit recopy overwrites the files this template lays
# but never deletes one, so removing it would leave every repo's old
# `exec just gate` in place; the recopy also reads a missing hooks/pre-push as
# a wiped surface (speckit_recopy HOOK_FILES).
echo "push: this branch's lanes are its gate: the door runs them on the cluster for the head you pushed (metered by daedalus); git_pr open parks on them, and repo_ci_logs reads them" >&2
exit 0
